~ Lava slice 10 — bounds: refinements declared on a container, using prose
~ comparators. A bound is part of the container's identity; the bad state can't exist.

~ literal bound: balance can never go negative
create container "Credit" of type int >= 0 with value 100

~ relational bound: a hold can never exceed the credit backing it
create container "Hold" of type int <= Credit with value 0

~ legal moves
update Credit to [Credit - 40]      ~ 60, still >= 0
update Hold to 60                    ~ 60, not greater than Credit (60)
print(Credit)
print(Hold)

~ a guarded effect that respects the bound
if (Credit is 60) then update Hold to [Hold - 10]
print(Hold)

~ the bad state is structurally impossible — see bounds-violation.lava (rejected)
~ and bounds-atomic.lava (a synchronous block may dip then commit consistent).
